"basis" 1381 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039809/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-113763" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "There is a local minimum at $x=1$"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039809/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d917355fdf0b7e7cf840cb941c0026d8d29be6c019240235c78373e87909d0a" "basis" 1381 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039809/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-49022" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For which value of $x$ does the function $f(x)={x}^{2}{e}^{x}$ have a local minimum?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039561/state.json" "file_sha256" "0fa56fb2fb1b39c09da5400ada2be39480c5cd39e7c82cff9132f18d00554df7" "basis" 1370 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039561/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-49022" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the stationary points. Differentiating $f(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={x}^{2}\\cdot {e}^{x}+2x{e}^{x}=(x+2)x{e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving ${f}^{′}(x)=0$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+2)x{e}^{x} & =0 \\\\ (x+2)x & =0 \\\\ x & =-2,0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $x=-2$ and $x=0$ are stationary points. Next, to determine whether these points are local maxima or minima, we use the first derivative test.\n\nLet's choose the test points $x=-3,-1,1$ and evaluate the first derivative at these points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(-3) & =(-3+2)(-3){e}^{-3}=3{e}^{-3}>0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(-1) & =(-1+2)(-1){e}^{-1}=-{e}^{-1}<0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(1) & =(1+2)(1){e}^{1}=3e>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe summarize the information in a table, shown below.\n\n| $x$ | $(-\\infty ,-2)$ | $-2$ | $(-2,0)$ | $0$ | $(0,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Test Point | $-3$ |  | $-1$ |  | $1$ |\n| ${f}^{′}$ | $+$ | $0$ | $-$ | $0$ | $+$ |\n| $f$ | $↗$ | max | $↘$ | min | $↗$ |\n\nFinally, let's use the table above to classify the critical points.\n\n- At $x=-2,$ the first derivative changes sign from positive to negative. Therefore, $x=-2$ is a local maximum.\n\n- At $x=0,$ the first derivative changes sign from negative to positive. Therefore, $x=0$ is a local minimum.\n\nWe conclude that $f(x)$ has a local minimum at $x=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039561/state.json" "file_sha256" "0fa56fb2fb1b39c09da5400ada2be39480c5cd39e7c82cff9132f18d00554df7" "basis" 1370 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039561/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-49022" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039561/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "75475ea4b7463cabcd8545f73218469ca3eaf032b72cf1e124f044def2dbf532" "basis" 1370 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039561/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-49022" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039561/state.json" "file_sha256" "0fa56fb2fb1b39c09da5400ada2be39480c5cd39e7c82cff9132f18d00554df7" "basis" 1370 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/1